WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.742
Status flags record properties of certain operation results.

00:00:03.742 --> 00:00:09.824
In the 8085, common flags include carry, zero, sign, parity and auxiliary carry.

00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:15.905
Each instruction’s flag effects must be checked; not every instruction changes every flag.

00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:18.749
The mathematical sum is 100H.

00:00:18.749 --> 00:00:21.332
A stores 00H and carry becomes 1.

00:00:21.332 --> 00:00:27.234
Zero becomes 1, sign becomes 0, and parity is even because zero has zero one bits.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:30.185
Auxiliary carry is also 1 for this addition.

00:00:31.185 --> 00:00:35.269
Is the number of one bits in 03H even?

00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:38.900
03H is 00000011, which has two set bits.
